WEBVTT


00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.100
Everyone talks about Japan versus Korea,

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:04.581
but no one really tells you how different they feel

00:00:04.582 --> 00:00:06.381
until you have done both back to back.

00:00:06.382 --> 00:00:08.421
Japan feels like a machine, clean,

00:00:08.422 --> 00:00:09.881
quiet, convenient.

00:00:09.882 --> 00:00:12.221
We lived of vending machines and convenience store. Ramen,

00:00:12.222 --> 00:00:13.901
Korea, total opposite.

00:00:13.902 --> 00:00:15.101
Loud, chaotic,

00:00:15.102 --> 00:00:16.901
Wi-Fi literally everywhere.

00:00:16.902 --> 00:00:19.501
And Seoul, best foods in we have ever been.

00:00:19.502 --> 00:00:21.141
Budget wise, Japan hit us hard.

00:00:21.142 --> 00:00:22.781
Fancy cafes, not happening.

00:00:22.782 --> 00:00:23.621
But in Busan,

00:00:23.622 --> 00:00:26.461
we hopped to different cafes and still stayed under budget.

00:00:26.462 --> 00:00:28.941
In Japan, we clung to 7 11 and McDonald's.

00:00:28.942 --> 00:00:31.661
In Korea, the option spoiled us. Honestly,

00:00:31.662 --> 00:00:33.781
Korea felt more social, more fun,

00:00:33.782 --> 00:00:36.861
but Japan gave us calm. The reset was kind of quiet.

00:00:36.862 --> 00:00:38.441
So if you're wondering which is better,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.380
here's the truth. You need both.

00:00:40.381 --> 00:00:42.021
To love the energy of Korea,

00:00:42.022 --> 00:00:43.781
you have to feel the stillness of Japan.

00:00:43.782 --> 00:00:46.181
And to really enjoy the softness of Japan,

00:00:46.182 --> 00:00:48.301
you need to live a little loud in Korea.

00:00:48.302 --> 00:00:49.901
Follow for more on established facts,

00:00:49.902 --> 00:00:51.386
not just the Instagrammable stuff.
